{"description":"M2 — project the binding index to where the agent reads, per host, generated and verified. Nested AGENTS.md per directory generated from the M1 binding index, plus per-host shims through the vehicle that already exists (eka-mcp configure --target claude|cursor|opencode producing .claude/rules/*.md with paths: and .cursor/rules/*.mdc with globs). Rules: minimal, specific, only the constraints that genuinely bind that subtree, never written by hand, always verified. Nested rather than one large file because nested loads on demand where the host supports it while a large file is a permanent prefix tax — and the 2026 evidence measures large context files lowering task success. The spike is whether path-scoped projection changes behaviour at all, which is not yet measured for any host: if it is neutral, this item drops in priority and the gate carries the load.","acceptanceCriteria":"- A command generates nested entry points from the binding index; regenerating is byte-identical and a hand-edited nested file fails the check.\n- Per-host shims are emitted for the declared targets only, and a target that is not configured is skipped rather than approximated.\n- Each generated nested file names only constraints whose scope matches that subtree, proven by a fixture repository with two subtrees bound by different constraints.\n- Files that would be empty are not written, so the projection does not litter a repository with stubs.\n- The spike result is recorded: an A/B on comparable tasks measuring constraint resolution rate, steps and cost, with the honest outcome stated even if it is neutral."}